      "title": "Battery Price in Nagpur 2026 — Complete Buying Guide",
      "slug": "battery-price-in-nagpur-2026",
      "excerpt": "Current car, bike and inverter battery prices in Nagpur with exchange vs without exchange, plus tips to avoid overpaying.",
      "coverImage": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1593941707882-a5bba14938c7?w=1200&q=80",
      "sections": [
        {
          "heading": "Why prices vary",
          "body": "Brand, Ah capacity, warranty and old-battery exchange value all affect the final amount. Always compare with-exchange vs without-exchange before deciding."
        },
        {
          "heading": "Car batteries",
          "body": "Hatchback batteries (35Ah) typically start from ₹4,499 with exchange. SUV batteries (60–65Ah) cost more — from ₹6,999 with exchange. We publish both prices on every product page."
        },
        {
          "heading": "Bike batteries",
          "body": "Most scooters use 5Ah VRLA starting from ₹1,399 with exchange. Bigger bikes may need 7–9Ah. Fitment is usually under 20 minutes at your doorstep."
        },
        {
          "heading": "Inverter batteries",
          "body": "Tubular batteries (150–200Ah) are preferred for Nagpur summers. 150Ah tubular starts from ₹12,499 with exchange. Factor in backup hours and inverter matching."
        },
        {
          "heading": "Localities we cover",
          "body": "Pardi, Sadar, Dharampeth, Sitabuldi, Hingna, Wardha Road and 20+ more — with locality-specific delivery ETAs."
        }
      ],
      "published": true
    },
    {
      "id": "2",
      "title": "How to Choose a Car Battery in Nagpur Heat",
      "slug": "choose-car-battery-nagpur-heat",
      "excerpt": "Ah rating, warranty and heat tolerance — what matters when summers hit 45°C in Nagpur.",
      "coverImage": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1486262715619-67b85e0b08d3?w=1200&q=80",
      "sections": [
        {
          "heading": "Heat stress on batteries",
          "body": "Nagpur summers stress car batteries. Choose adequate Ah for your vehicle, prefer brands with strong heat performance, and replace before monsoon if cranking is weak."
        },
        {
          "heading": "What to check",
          "body": "Check CCA (Cold Cranking Amps), reserve capacity, and warranty period. Maintenance-free batteries are best for city driving."
        }
      ],
      "published": true
    },
    {
